                  "content": "SELECTED: candidate_65\n\nCONFIDENCE: HIGH\n\nEXPLANATION:\nThe fix commit changes `addBootCP` in src/polyglot/main/Options.java from\n`bootclasspathDirectories().addAll(value);` to\n`bootclasspathDirectories().addAll(0, value);`, i.e. it makes the added\npaths get prepended to the bootclasspath list instead of appended.\n\ncandidate_65 is the commit that first introduces the `addBootCP` method\n(and the corresponding `-addbootcp` command-line flag). The flag's own\nhelp text explicitly says it should \"prepend <path> to the bootclasspath\",\nbut the method body implemented in this commit is:\n\n    protected void addBootCP(List<File> value) {\n        bootclasspath_directories.addAll(value);\n    }\n\nThis appends rather than prepends, directly contradicting the documented\nbehavior of the flag and matching precisely the defect that the fix\ncommit later corrects (by switching to `addAll(0, value)`). No other\ncandidate introduces or first touches this method \u2014 the remaining\nmatches (candidates 66, 67, 72, 78, 80, 85) only involve later,\nunrelated modifications to the surrounding code/refactors of the field\nname (bootclasspath_directories -> bootclasspathDirectories()) without\nchanging this append semantics. Therefore candidate_65 is the\nbug-introducing commit.\n"
